{title: Let All Mortal Flesh Keep Silence}
{artist: Liturgy of St. James, tr. Gerard Moultrie / Picardy (French carol)}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Let_All_Mortal_Flesh_Keep_Silence-Picardy)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Let all mortal flesh [Bb]keep [Dm]silence,
[Dm]And with [Bb]fear and [Gm]trem[C]bling [F]stand;
[Bb]Ponder nothing [Dm]earth[Gm]ly [Dm]minded,
[Dm]For with [C7]bles[F]sing [Bb]in His [A]hand,
[D]Christ our God to [Gm]earth de[Dm]scend[Am]eth,
[Dm]Our full homage [G]to [C]de[Dm]mand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]King of kings, yet born [Bb]of [Dm]Mary,
[Dm]As of [Bb]old on [Gm]earth [C]He [F]stood,
[Bb]Lord of lords, in [Dm]hu[Gm]man [Dm]vesture,
[Dm]In the [C7]bo[F]dy [Bb]and the [A]blood;
[D]He will give to [Gm]all the [Dm]fai[Am]thful
[Dm]His own self for [G]hea[C]venly [Dm]food.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Rank on rank the host [Bb]of [Dm]Heaven
[Dm]Spreads its [Bb]vanguard [Gm]on [C]the [F]way,
[Bb]As the Light of [Dm]light [Gm]de[Dm]scendeth
[Dm]From the [C7]realms [F]of [Bb]endless [A]day,
[D]That the powers of [Gm]hell may [Dm]va[Am]nish
[Dm]As the darkness [G]clears [C]a[Dm]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]At His feet the six [Bb]wingèd [Dm]seraph,
[Dm]Cheru[Bb]bim with [Gm]sleep[C]less [F]eye,
[Bb]Veil their faces [Dm]to [Gm]the [Dm]presence,
[Dm]As with [C7]cease[F]less [Bb]voice they [A]cry:
[D]Allelu[Gm]ia, Al[Dm]lelu[Am]ia
[Dm]Alleluia, [G]Lord [C]Most [Dm]High!
{end_of_verse}
